    "description": "Download one remote regular file through the existing SSH SFTP connection with independent remote-read and local-write grants. Supply current scope/resource revisions and epoch, a single remoteName and a relative local destination path. Never overwrites an existing local target, opens a new connection or executes a file. Reuse query_transfer/cancel_transfer and retain operationId; retries must keep the same direction and arguments. published/publication and temporary describe the local destination and owned local temporary file. Size and metadata checks do not verify content hashes. Current native local writer is Windows-only; maximum 64 MiB, 64 KiB chunks, 120 seconds overall and 15 seconds without progress between synchronous calls. Remote path checks trust the authorized directory owner and administrator; SFTPv3 cannot prove isolation from same-account malicious path replacement.",
